<title>PAKISTAN: KARACHI PORT HANDLES 89,086 TONNES CARGO.</title>
<headline>KARACHI PORT HANDLES 89,086 TONNES CARGO.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 89,086 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday, compared to 69,228 tonnes on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Thursday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			  17,091	   10,711</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  71,995	   58,517</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, five ships are expected to sail and seven to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Steel		    4,942	 Pericles	     due</p>
<p>Palm oil		 7,774	 Fossanger	    due</p>
<p>Veg Oil		  18,600	Kristal		due</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,155	Rong Jiang	   due</p>
<p>Rock/Phosphate	 27,000	Philadalphia	 8/8</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
